+## Unverified or open items
+
+- **QUIC vs. a hand-rolled SSP datagram layer** was not researched. Successor claims (RoSE, oxutrm, qsh, morsh, quosh, SSH3) come from READMEs and blogs only.
+- **WezTerm mux internals** were not read in source: the remote daemon channel, PDU framing, and local-echo repair. They are worth reading before designing herdr's prediction layer.
+- **Prediction threshold history**: git history of the `SRTT_TRIGGER`/`FLAG_TRIGGER` constants was not checked. Older secondary sources may quote other values.
+- **Modern-shell misprediction cases** (zsh right prompts, autosuggest, tmux status lines) were not surveyed in mosh issues.
+- **PMTUD on macOS/BSD**, where `IP_MTU_DISCOVER` is absent, is unverified. The value of `IPV6_HEADER_LEN` (64 per the transport note) was not re-read for this report.
+- **Linux suspend/wake** behaviour is inferred from code and OS semantics, not tested.
+- **VS Code Remote-SSH** details are from memory.
+- **herdr specifics**: how herdr frames screen updates today (full redraw vs. diffs, stream vs. latest-wins) and whether libghostty-vt can provide cheap row identity. These decide the effort column for #1 and come from the herdr-side investigation.
